Preheat the oven to 175°C (350°F) and line a 9x13” pan. Put the cocoa powder, chopped chocolate and espresso powder in a heatproof bowl. Brown the butter in a saucepan over medium-low heat, stirring often, until the milk solids turn brown and smell nutty, then immediately pour it over the cocoa mixture and stir until smooth; set aside to cool. Whip the sugars, vanilla and eggs until thick and pale (4-10 minutes), then slowly pour in the cooled chocolate-butter mixture. Fold in the flour and salt until just combined – the batter will be thick. Spread into the pan and bake for about 25 minutes until the top is glossy and just set. Do not overbake – they finish cooking as they cool. Let cool at least 30 minutes before slicing.

