Preheat the oven to 150°C (fan) and line a 6” cake tin. Whip the egg whites, gradually adding the sugar, until soft peaks form. Whisk in the egg yolks by hand, then sift in the cake flour and salt and fold through. Warm the milk and oil together and fold in, along with the vanilla and pandan paste. Pour into the tin, tap out any air bubbles, and bake for 40 minutes. For the cream: hydrate the gelatin in water and melt it, whip the cream with the sugar, then fold in the gelatin. Top the cooled cake with the cream and sprinkle with toasted coconut.

