Cream the sugar, shortening, molasses and egg together. Sift the dry ingredients and beat them in, along with the milk. Drop by the tablespoonful onto greased sheets and press down lightly with a floured glass. Bake in a moderate oven until set, but do not overbake.

Bagels
Recipe from Adapted from thia.codes
Base recipe serves 11.

viewof bagels_servings = Inputs.range(
  [1, 22], {value: 11, step: 1, label: "Servings"}
)







bagels_base = ({
  servings: 11,
  ingredients: [{"name":"Bread flour, ~10% protein","amount":953,"unit":"g"},{"name":"Vital wheat gluten","amount":47,"unit":"g"},{"name":"Diastatic malt powder","amount":2.5,"unit":"g"},{"name":"Water","amount":500,"unit":"g"},{"name":"Instant yeast","amount":5,"unit":"g"},{"name":"Salt","amount":25,"unit":"g"},{"name":"Neutral oil, e.g. grapeseed or sunflower","amount":30,"unit":"g"},{"name":"Dark brown sugar","amount":50,"unit":"g"},{"name":"Barley malt syrup, for boiling water","amount":1,"unit":"Tbsp"}]
})







