Whisk the flour and vital wheat gluten together, then stir in the diastatic malt powder, instant yeast, salt and brown sugar. Add the water and oil and knead by hand for about 10 minutes. Cover and rest 20 minutes, then knead again for 10 minutes - then allow to rise till ~1.5-2x in size. Divide into ~120g pieces, roll each into a snake, wrap around your hand and roll firmly against the counter to seal. Rest at room temperature, covered, until a bagel floats when dropped in water (about an hour), then refrigerate 16-24 hours (they’ll keep up to ~3 days). The next day, heat the oven as hot as possible, boil a jug of water and also bring a pot of water to a gentle boil with the malt syrup stirred in.
Place a tray with a tea towel on it in the base of your oven and cover in boiling water - then place in oven. Then boil the bagels 10-15 seconds per side, then arrange face-down on an oven tray with baking paper or a silpat, and then bake for ~20 minutes.
